# Reusable AI project instructions

## How to work with the user

- Act as senior Java / tech lead; use Spec-Driven Development end-to-end.
- Workflow: **Requirement → Specification → Plan/Tasks → Implementation → Testing → Review → Fix**.
- **Never** start by building the complete application in one shot.
- **Confirm with the user** before acting on doubts, open questions, or non-obvious judgments.
- Prefer **graphify** for codebase exploration when `graphify-out/` exists (`.cursor/rules/graphify.mdc`). Keep static rules in `rules/` + pointer `.mdc` files for prompt caching.

## Artefacts to maintain

| Artefact | Location |
|----------|----------|
| Rules (source of truth) | `rules/*.md` |
| Rules (Cursor pointers) | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` — do not duplicate bodies |
| Commands | `commands/*.md`; `.cursor/commands/*.md` pointers only |
| Specs before code | `spec/` — see `rules/documentation.md` for the full list and `architecture.md` section map |
| Prompt history | SpecStory → `.specstory/history/`; index `docs/prompt-history.md` |
| AI mistakes (PDF) | `docs/ai-mistakes.md` when at least one meaningful mistake is caught |
| RAG eval approach | `spec/evaluation-strategy.md` (retrieval quality — not unit golden strings) |

**Commands:** `review-code`, `review-frontend`, `review-spec`, `generate-tests`, `review-rag-output`.

## When reviewing AI output

- **Backend code:** `commands/review-code.md` against specs + `rules/*`.
- **UI code:** `commands/review-frontend.md` — no frontend tests this milestone.
- **Specs:** `commands/review-spec.md` before implementation.
- **Ask answers:** `commands/review-rag-output.md` — every claim traceable to cited ticket ids from retrieval; honest no-match when nothing relevant.
- **Tests:** `commands/generate-tests.md` — backend only.
- Prefer these commands over ad-hoc “looks fine”.
- Document meaningful mistakes per `rules/documentation.md`.

## Assessment PDF (local)

Authoritative assignment: `docs/Assessments.pdf` (gitignored). Extract into `spec/requirements.md`. Distinguish **PDF requirement** vs **project convention** in every rule file’s opening sections.
